      "reason": "Determine how to preserve baseline behavior and isolate improvements from normalization changes.",
      "query": "For SASRec augmented with z = LayerNorm(h + g * LayerNorm(recency_pool(item_embeddings))), what residual initialization and normalization controls preserve the baseline at initialization? Investigate zero-initialized residual gates, small sigmoid-gate gradients, and normalization-only ablations in sequential recommendation and residual Transformers."
    },
    {
      "reason": "Check whether the proposed mechanism addresses temporal intent or introduces a similarity shortcut.",
      "query": "In Amazon sequential recommendation, what evidence distinguishes gains from exponentially weighted recent-item pooling from item-similarity and popularity shortcuts? Compare event-order versus elapsed-time decay, repeat versus nonrepeat targets, history-length slices, and simple last-item or fixed-pooling baselines using training-only histories."
    },
